      "content": "# HVAC Installation and Repair in Brooklyn, NY\nOur home base. Heating and cooling for brownstones, co-ops, new condos and storefronts across the borough.\nOur home base\n## Your Local HVAC Contractor in Brooklyn\nMode Mechanical is based in Brooklyn, and most of our work happens here — from a single ductless unit in a top-floor walk-up to rooftop condensers for a mixed-use building.\nBrooklyn’s housing stock is unusually varied, so the right system depends on the building. Before we quote, we look at how the space is heated today, where an outdoor unit can legally and practically go, and how refrigerant lines or ducts can be routed without tearing up original details.\n### Neighborhoods we serve in Brooklyn\n- Park Slope\n- Bed-Stuy\n- Williamsburg\n- Greenpoint\n- Fort Greene\n- Clinton Hill\n- Crown Heights\n- Prospect Heights\n- Bushwick\n- Bay Ridge\n- Sunset Park\n- Flatbush\nDon’t see yours? Call (914) 223-3301 and we’ll tell you straight away.\n## Homes and Buildings We Work On in Brooklyn\n### Brownstones and row houses\nMost were built without ductwork and heat with a boiler and radiators. Ductless mini-splits or small-duct systems add cooling (and efficient heat) floor by floor, with condensers on the roof or in the rear yard.\n### Pre-war co-ops and walk-ups\nWindow units and through-wall sleeves are common. Boards usually want to approve outdoor unit placement first, so we plan the installation around the building’s rules.\n### New condos and conversions\nNewer buildings often use VRF systems, heat pumps or fan coils. We service, repair and replace these systems and their controls.\n### Storefronts and restaurants\nRooftop units, split systems and ventilation for retail, offices and food service — with work scheduled to keep your business open.\n## HVAC Services in Brooklyn\n- Installation Central air, furnaces, boilers and heat pumps, sized to the building and installed to code.\n- Maintenance Annual tune-ups that keep systems efficient and catch problems before they become breakdowns.\n- Repair AC and heating repair with a written price before any work starts, and 24/7 emergency service.\n## Questions from Brooklyn Customers\n### Can you add air conditioning to a brownstone with no ductwork?\nYes. Ductless mini-splits are the usual answer: small indoor heads in each room, slim refrigerant lines run through closets or along the exterior, and an outdoor condenser on the roof or in the yard. They heat as well as cool, so they can also take load off an old boiler.\n### Do I need co-op or condo board approval for a new system?\nUsually, yes. Most boards want to approve where the outdoor unit goes and see the contractor’s paperwork before work starts. Tell us early and we’ll plan the installation around the board’s requirements.\n## Other Areas We Serve\n- HVAC in Queens\n- HVAC in Manhattan\n- HVAC in the Bronx\n- HVAC on Staten Island\n- HVAC on Long Island\n- HVAC in Westchester County"
